gist, by Semantic Arts
----------------------

This product includes and is derived from gist 14.1.0, the upper ontology
for the enterprise created and published by Semantic Arts:
https://www.semanticarts.com/gist/ and https://github.com/semanticarts/gist

gist is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
license (CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

- upstream/gist14.1.0_webDownload/ holds the release unmodified, with its
  LICENSE.txt.
- tests/vendor/semanticarts/ holds ontologyShapes.ttl and
  property_type_construct.rq, copied unmodified from the validation/
  folder of semanticarts/gist, with its LICENSE.txt.
- src/gist/schema/, src/gist/datamodel/, project/ and the gist-linkml
  package are adapted material. Changes made: the OWL modules
  are converted to LinkML by scripts/gist_to_linkml.py, their RDFS
  annotations and subclass assertions are folded into the schema, SSSOM
  mappings to other vocabularies are merged in, and the LinkML toolchain
  generates the other artefacts from the result.

Every gist class, property and individual keeps its Semantic Arts IRI under
https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/ (gist:) and
https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/data/gist/ (gistd:). This project defines
no terms in those namespaces; what it adds lives under
https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/ (gist_linkml:).

This is not an official Semantic Arts release, and its use does not imply
endorsement by Semantic Arts. For reasoning over gist itself, use Semantic
Arts' own OWL release.

SSSOM mappings
--------------

The mapping sets under src/gist/mappings/ are this project's work, licensed
under CC BY 4.0 as each file's header states. They relate gist terms to the
LinkML renderings of the FINOS Common Domain Model, DPVs and ISO/IEC
22989:2022 published under https://w3id.org/lmodel/. Those vocabularies
remain the work of their own authors under their own terms; the mappings
cite their terms by identifier and reproduce none of their text. They are
this project's interpretation, not an official alignment by any of those
bodies or by Semantic Arts.

